#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064009 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/id #uuid "4d4edfc8-e178-58b4-b827-e4310ead130e" :question/math-academy-id "e-485" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 \\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1}\\,\\textrm d x$." :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\color{red}-1$ | $4$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1} = 4 -\\dfrac{5}{x+1}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{1}\\frac{4x - 1}{x + 1}dx &= ∫_{0}^{1}(4 - \\frac{5}{x + 1})dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}4dx - 5∫_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x + 1}dx \\\\\n&= 4x\\begin{vmatrix}_{0}^{1} - 5\\ln & x + 1\\end{vmatrix} \\mid _{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= [4 - 0] - 5[\\ln 2 - \\ln 1] \\\\\n&= 4 - 5\\ln 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064010 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/id #uuid "74761123-d539-5d78-8dcd-4ea1db04bed0" :question/math-academy-id "e-486" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{2x^2-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\textrm d x$." :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^2$ | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\color{red}3$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n|  | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{2x^2-3x-4}{x-3} = 2x + 3 + \\dfrac {5}{x-3}. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{2x^{2} - 3x - 4}{x - 3}dx &= ∫(2x + 3 + \\frac{5}{x - 3})dx \\\\\n&= x^{2} + 3x + 5\\ln \\mid x - 3 \\mid + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064011 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "cf016fa7-c3a2-5f9b-84a6-7b005d0d7286" :question/math-academy-id "e-487" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\textrm d x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{x - 1}{2x - 1}dx &= ∫(x - 1)/(2(x - \\frac{1}{2}))dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫(x - 1)/((x - \\frac{1}{2}))dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\color{red}\\dfrac12$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $\\dfrac12$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-\\dfrac12$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 1)/((x - \\frac{1}{2})) &= 1 - ((\\frac{1}{2}))/((x - \\frac{1}{2})) \\\\\n&= 1 - (1)/(2(x - \\frac{1}{2})) \\\\\n&= 1 - \\frac{1}{2x - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{x - 1}{2x - 1}dx &= \\frac{1}{2}∫(1 - \\frac{1}{2x - 1})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}[x - \\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}2x - 1 & ] + C \\\\ = \\frac{1}{2}x - \\frac{1}{4}\\ln & 2x - 1\\end{vmatrix}+ C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6ec7aa7-5704-5568-870c-5ce10aacd246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063215} {:answer/id #uuid "0696118c-8d16-57bc-84f9-e194e1db5ed6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + 4\\ln 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063216} {:answer/id #uuid "07a57a23-ffe8-5b87-b518-04162c920b8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063217} {:answer/id #uuid "3ab8157c-2a73-5169-9c52-b0b3c1080178" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2} + 3\\ln 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063218} {:answer/id #uuid "6eb36860-7c3a-5cc7-a89a-742e3848ffba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 - \\frac{7}{4}\\ln 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6eb36860-7c3a-5cc7-a89a-742e3848ffba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 - \\frac{7}{4}\\ln 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063219} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bff75e6-1700-5d80-adcb-dc6641c8c8b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063214}] :question/id #uuid "1aaedd48-8858-5316-b8f3-55fab9e40276" :question/math-academy-id "q-49467" :question/problem "Evaluate $∫_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x - 1}{2x + 1}dx$."}]}
